window.docContents[102].resolve({"/part-1-foundations/ch01-what-are-the-hyperreals/#Lectures-on-the-Hyperreals-___-Interactive-Lean-4-___-Spatial-Edition--Part-I-___-Foundations-of-the-Hyperreal-Line--Chapter-1___-What-Are-the-Hyperreals___--Field-Agnostic-Infinitesimal-Arithmetic":{"contents":"In Ch01_WhatAreTheHyperreals.lean, we first develop Goldblatt's §1.2–§1.4 axiomatic laws inside any strict ordered field extending \\mathbb{R} ([Field F] [LinearOrder F] [IsStrictOrderedRing F]). Even before constructing \\mathbb{R}^*, the order axioms alone force:\n\n* 0 is the only real number that is infinitesimal; if a subfield contains a nonzero infinitesimal \\varepsilon, its reciprocal \\varepsilon^{-1} is infinite (exceeding every standard real in absolute value), and the field cannot be Archimedean.* Infinitesimals form an additive group closed under multiplication by any limited element, whereas \\infty - \\infty and \\varepsilon / \\delta remain genuinely indeterminate—for example, \\varepsilon^2 / \\varepsilon = \\varepsilon \\approx 0, \\varepsilon / \\varepsilon = 1, and \\varepsilon / \\varepsilon^2 = \\varepsilon^{-1} is unlimited.\n\nHover or tap any identifier in the live-elaborated Lean 4 block below to inspect its exact kernel type and proof state:\n\nsection\nopen Goldblatt.Ch01\n\n-- Every nonzero infinitesimal has an infinite reciprocal, and vice versa:\n#check @isNonzeroInfinitesimalIn_iff_inv_isInfiniteIn\n\n-- Sums of infinitesimals remain infinitesimal in any ordered field:\nexample {F : Type*} [Field F] [LinearOrder F] [IsStrictOrderedRing F]\n    {ε δ : F} (hε : IsInfinitesimalIn ε) (hδ : IsInfinitesimalIn δ) :\n    IsInfinitesimalIn (ε + δ) :=\n  hε.add hδ\nend\n\n\n","context":"Lectures on the Hyperreals — Interactive Lean 4 & Spatial Edition\u0009Part I — Foundations of the Hyperreal Line\u0009Chapter 1: What Are the Hyperreals?","header":"1.1.1. Field-Agnostic Infinitesimal Arithmetic","id":"/part-1-foundations/ch01-what-are-the-hyperreals/#Lectures-on-the-Hyperreals-___-Interactive-Lean-4-___-Spatial-Edition--Part-I-___-Foundations-of-the-Hyperreal-Line--Chapter-1___-What-Are-the-Hyperreals___--Field-Agnostic-Infinitesimal-Arithmetic"}});